sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant ALB as Application<br/>Load Balancer
    participant App as storefront<br/>(private subnet)
    participant IMDS as IMDSv2
    participant VPCE as DynamoDB<br/>gateway endpoint
    participant DDB as DynamoDB
    participant CW as CloudWatch

    Note over App,IMDS: At boot, once
    App->>IMDS: PUT /latest/api/token
    IMDS-->>App: session token (IMDSv1 is disabled)
    App->>IMDS: GET instance-id, AZ, instance-type
    IMDS-->>App: i-0abc... · us-east-1a · t4g.micro

    Note over App,DDB: Every 60s, in the background
    App->>VPCE: dynamodb:Scan (instance role credentials)
    VPCE->>DDB: routed over the AWS network,<br/>never via the NAT Gateway
    DDB-->>App: 6 catalog items
    App->>App: cache in memory

    Note over User,CW: Per request
    User->>ALB: GET /
    ALB->>App: forward to a healthy target
    App-->>ALB: 200 + X-Instance-Id, X-Availability-Zone
    ALB-->>User: storefront page

    Note over App,CW: The catalog is served from memory,<br/>so a request never blocks on DynamoDB
    App->>CW: structured JSON log line
    ALB->>CW: RequestCount, TargetResponseTime, 5xx

    Note over ALB,App: Health check, every 5s per target
    ALB->>App: GET /health
    App-->>ALB: 200 — deliberately shallow

    Note over App: /health does NOT check DynamoDB.<br/>A deep check would fail every instance at once<br/>when a shared dependency broke, turning a<br/>degraded feature into a total outage.
